{
 "about": "The paper gives the scans per day but not when they were taken. Each day's packages are put back to back, centred on the Sun's transit at G\u00f6ttingen, and that stretch is cut into hour-long nodes (at least one), each weighted by its share of the day's scans, with its own air mass and v_r at its midpoint. Each day gets the ERA5 profile at 11 UTC (transit is at ~11:20 UTC on these dates): The NIR setting (``--setting nir``) is the same construction on its own six days, 1130 scans, with a package of 10 taking ~17 min (the longer scan of its 0.0044 cm-1 resolution); the two settings were never observed on the same day:",
 "source": "Reiners et al. 2016, A&A 587, A65, Table 2 (NIR)",
